{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":8,"lang":"pl","title":"Umiem, możesz, zrób","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Czego się nauczysz","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"W tej lekcji uczysz się mówić, co umiesz, a czego nie: «umiem szyć», «nie umiem jeździć na łyżwach». A także prosić: «możesz pożyczyć mi długopis?», dawać krótkie polecenia: «podłącz to» — i mówić «nie rób»: «nie spiesz się»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can sew.","translation":"Umiem szyć.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can't skate.","translation":"Nie umiem jeździć na łyżwach.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"Can you lend me a pen?","translation":"Możesz pożyczyć mi długopis?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Plug it in.","translation":"Podłącz to.","hi":"Plug"},{"en":"Don't rush.","translation":"Nie spiesz się.","hi":"Don't"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"can — «umiem», «mogę»","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"can stoi między kto a czynnością: I can sew — «umiem szyć». Po can czynność jest w formie słownikowej: bez to i bez s. I nie zapomnij o I: «umiem szyć» to I can sew, a nie Can sew."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"can","accent":true},{"text":"czynność jak w słowniku","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can sew.","translation":"Umiem szyć.","hi":"can"},{"en":"He can dance.","translation":"On umie tańczyć.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can speak English.","translation":"Mówię po angielsku.","hi":"can"},{"en":"He can edit photos.","translation":"On umie obrabiać zdjęcia.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can polish shoes.","translation":"Ona umie pastować buty.","hi":"can"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Can sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"I can to sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"I can sews.","right":"I can sew."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"I can","after":"English.","options":["speak","to speak","speaks"],"answer":"speak","why":"Po can czynność bez to i bez s."}}]},{"num":"03","title":"can się nie zmienia","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"W lekcji 6 po he i she czynność dostawała s. Z can — nie: ani can, ani czynność po nim się nie zmieniają. He can dance, a nie He cans dance ani He can dances."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"He can dance.","translation":"On umie tańczyć.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can polish shoes.","translation":"Ona umie pastować buty.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can check the rating.","translation":"Ona może sprawdzić ocenę.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can give feedback.","translation":"Ona może dać informację zwrotną.","hi":"can"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"He cans dance.","right":"He can dance."},{"wrong":"He can dances.","right":"He can dance."},{"wrong":"She can to climb.","right":"She can climb."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"spot_slip","kind":"spot_slip","chips":["He","can","dances"],"answerIndex":2,"hint":"Jedno słowo ma zbędną końcówkę. Dotknij go.","fix":"Po can czynność bez s: He can dance."}}]},{"num":"04","title":"can't — «nie umiem», «nie mogę»","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «nie» stoi przed czasownikiem: «nie umiem». Po angielsku przeczenie przykleja się do can: can't. I can't skate — «nie umiem jeździć na łyżwach». Ani I not can, ani I don't can."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can't skate.","translation":"Nie umiem jeździć na łyżwach.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"She can't ski.","translation":"Ona nie umie jeździć na nartach.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"He can't dive.","translation":"On nie umie nurkować.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"I can't make the bed.","translation":"Nie mogę pościelić łóżka.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"She can't do the ironing.","translation":"Ona nie może wyprasować prania.","hi":"can't"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I not can skate.","right":"I can't skate."},{"wrong":"I don't can skate.","right":"I can't skate."},{"wrong":"She can't skis.","right":"She can't ski."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Nie umiesz jeździć na łyżwach. Które zdanie jest poprawne?","optionA":"I not can skate.","optionB":"I can't skate.","correct":"B","explain":"Z can «nie» to can't."}}]},{"num":"05","title":"Zapytać «umiesz?» — Can you…?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Żeby zapytać, czy ktoś coś umie, can idzie na początek: Can you sew? Do nie jest potrzebne: can samo robi pytanie. Krótka odpowiedź: Yes, I can — «tak, umiem»."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"Can","accent":true},{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"czynność","accent":false},{"text":"?","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Can you sew?","translation":"Umiesz szyć?","hi":"Can"},{"en":"Can you hike?","translation":"Chodzisz po górach?","hi":"Can"},{"en":"Yes, I can.","translation":"Tak, umiem.","hi":"can"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"You can swim?","right":"Can you swim?"},{"wrong":"Do you can swim?","right":"Can you swim?"},{"wrong":"Yes, I can swim it.","right":"Yes, I can."}]}]},{"num":"06","title":"Prośba: Can you…?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"To samo pytanie — Can you…? — działa jak prośba: Can you lend me a pen? — «możesz pożyczyć mi długopis?». Po polsku też prosimy przez «możesz?», więc tu wszystko jest znajome."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Can you lend me a pen?","translation":"Możesz pożyczyć mi długopis?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you unfasten the strap?","translation":"Możesz odpiąć pasek?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you check the buckle?","translation":"Możesz sprawdzić klamrę?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you explain it?","translation":"Możesz to wyjaśnić?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you explain the diagram?","translation":"Możesz wyjaśnić schemat?","hi":"Can you"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Can you to explain it?","right":"Can you explain it?"},{"wrong":"You can lend me a pen?","right":"Can you lend me a pen?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Poproś: «Możesz wyjaśnić schemat?»","answer":["Can","you","explain","the","diagram"],"distractors":["to","Do"]}}]},{"num":"07","title":"Krótkie polecenie: czynność na początku","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Żeby powiedzieć «zrób», zaczyna się od razu od czynności, bez kto: Plug it in — «podłącz to», Buy semi-skimmed milk — «kup mleko półtłuste». To zwykła codzienna prośba, nie brzmi niegrzecznie."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"czynność","accent":false},{"text":"co","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Plug it in.","translation":"Podłącz to.","hi":"Plug"},{"en":"Plug in the humidifier.","translation":"Podłącz nawilżacz.","hi":"Plug"},{"en":"Turn on the shredder.","translation":"Włącz niszczarkę.","hi":"Turn on"},{"en":"Buy low-fat yoghurt.","translation":"Kup jogurt light.","hi":"Buy"},{"en":"Buy semi-skimmed milk.","translation":"Kup mleko półtłuste.","hi":"Buy"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"To plug it in.","right":"Plug it in."}]}]},{"num":"08","title":"«Nie rób»: Don't…","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Żeby powiedzieć «nie rób», przed czynnością stawia się Don't: Don't rush — «nie spiesz się». Not rush i No rush nie działają. Uprzejmiej — Please na początku: Please don't interrupt."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"(Please)","accent":false},{"text":"Don't","accent":true},{"text":"czynność","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Don't rush.","translation":"Nie spiesz się.","hi":"Don't"},{"en":"Don't lean on it.","translation":"Nie opieraj się o to.","hi":"Don't"},{"en":"Please don't interrupt.","translation":"Proszę, nie przerywaj.","hi":"Please don't"},{"en":"Don't spill it.","translation":"Nie rozlej tego.","hi":"Don't"},{"en":"Don't panic.","translation":"Nie panikuj.","hi":"Don't"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Not rush.","right":"Don't rush."},{"wrong":"No panic.","right":"Don't panic."},{"wrong":"Don't please interrupt.","right":"Please don't interrupt."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"panic.","options":["No","Not","Don't"],"answer":"Don't","why":"«Nie rób» to Don't przed czynnością."}}]},{"num":"09","title":"can — także «mogę pomóc», «możemy zrobić»","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"can to nie tylko «umiem». Tym samym słowem proponuje się pomoc i mówi o możliwościach: I can manage the list — «mogę prowadzić listę», We can share the workload — «możemy podzielić się pracą»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can evaluate it.","translation":"Mogę to ocenić.","hi":"can"},{"en":"We can choose a criterion.","translation":"Możemy wybrać kryterium.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can manage the list.","translation":"Mogę prowadzić listę.","hi":"can"},{"en":"We can share the workload.","translation":"Możemy podzielić się pracą.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can improve it.","translation":"Mogę to poprawić.","hi":"can"}]}]},{"num":"10","title":"Błędy, które robi prawie każdy","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Can sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"I can to sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"He can dances.","right":"He can dance."},{"wrong":"I not can skate.","right":"I can't skate."},{"wrong":"You can swim?","right":"Can you swim?"},{"wrong":"Not rush.","right":"Don't rush."},{"wrong":"Don't please interrupt.","right":"Please don't interrupt."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"can działa jak kłódka na czynności: po nim czynność zawsze jest jak w słowniku. Ani to, ani s, ani do."}]},{"num":"11","title":"Co zabrać do ćwiczeń","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"«Umiem, mogę» — I can + czynność jak w słowniku. «Nie umiem» — can't. «Umiesz? Możesz?» — Can you…? «Zrób» — czynność na początku. «Nie rób» — Don't…, uprzejmie — Please don't…"},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can speak English.","translation":"Mówię po angielsku.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can't ski.","translation":"Ona nie umie jeździć na nartach.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"Can you check the buckle?","translation":"Możesz sprawdzić klamrę?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Turn on the shredder.","translation":"Włącz niszczarkę.","hi":"Turn on"},{"en":"Please don't interrupt.","translation":"Proszę, nie przerywaj.","hi":"Please don't"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{}}
